# Secrets / external config (never commit)
#
# NOTE: app/google-services.json IS committed on purpose. It ships as a placeholder with fake
# identifiers so the project builds and runs out of the box (demo mode). Google's own guidance is
# that google-services.json is client configuration, not a secret — the protection comes from API-key
# restrictions and from the security rules, not from hiding this file. If you drop in a real one and
# would rather not commit it, add it here and adjust the README accordingly.
.env
*.keystore
*.jks
serviceAccountKey.json
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
firestore-debug.log
ui-debug.log

# Node (backend functions)
node_modules/
functions/node_modules/
rules-tests/node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/

